---
import LabCard from '../../components/LabCard.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getLabs } from '../../lib/labs';

const labs = await getLabs();
---

<Base
	title="Labs"
	description="Lab 01, Secret Exfiltration, is a draft local kind lab. Two more labs are placeholders."
	current="labs"
>
	<section class="section lab">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="kicker">Index</p>
			<h1>Labs</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Educate by doing. Lab 01 attacks a bare agent, repeats the attack inside an Agent Substrate actor, and
				scores the difference from the cluster. All lab attacks run only on a local kind cluster.
			</p>
			<ul class="lab-grid">
				{
					labs.map((lab) => (
						<li>
							<LabCard lab={lab} level={2} />
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>

			<div class="panel author">
				<h2>Add a lab</h2>
				<p>
					A published lab is a folder under <code>labs/</code>. The page shape is the
					<a href="/labs/template/">template</a>. Lab 01 is the example.
				</p>
				<ol>
					<li>
						Add <code>labs/NN-short-name/lab.md</code> with <code>title</code>, <code>slug</code>, <code>status</code>,
						and optional <code>duration</code> and <code>difficulty</code>. The site shows that status.
						<code>draft</code> is not "coming soon".
					</li>
					<li>
						Add <code>labs/NN-short-name/README.md</code>. Keep these level-2 headings, in order: Objectives,
						Prerequisites, Setup, Attack, Defend, Measure, Cleanup. Extra sections are fine. The site renders this
						file at <code>/labs/NN-short-name/</code>.
					</li>
					<li>
						Remove any placeholder at <code>site/src/content/labs/NN-short-name.md</code>. A placeholder is only for a
						lab that does not have a repo folder yet.
					</li>
					<li>
						From <code>site/</code>, run <code>npm run build</code>. The build fails if a required heading is missing,
						or if site copy contains an em dash or an en dash.
					</li>
				</ol>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
